{
  "slug": "everhour",
  "name": "Everhour",
  "description": "Track time in Everhour from your AI: find tasks, log and correct time, start and stop timers, and read projects, clients, team time records, invoices, expenses, the schedule and project and user reports.",
  "instructions": "## Everhour\nThis connector calls the **Everhour API** (`https://api.everhour.com`) with the user's own API key: users, projects, tasks, clients, time records, timers, invoices, expenses, the resource planner and the projects and users reports. It can log time, change a time record and start or stop a timer; deleting a time record is installed switched off.\n\n**Writes need a yes.** Before `everhour_add_time`, `everhour_update_time_record`, `everhour_start_timer` or `everhour_stop_timer`, tell the user what will be recorded (task, day, duration, comment) and wait for their confirmation. Time records feed invoices and payroll, so never guess a task or a duration.\n\n**Setup (about 1 minute)**\n1. Sign in at https://app.everhour.com and open **Settings, My Profile** (https://app.everhour.com/#/account/profile).\n2. Copy the **API Token** at the bottom of the page into `EVERHOUR_API_KEY`. It is sent as the `X-Api-Key` header and only to api.everhour.com. The key acts as you: members see their own data, admins see the team.\n\n**Units**: time is always in **seconds** (3600 = 1 hour) and money in **cents** (500 = 5.00). Dates are `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n**IDs**: projects and tasks carry their platform prefix, `ev:` for Everhour itself and `as:` (Asana), `tr:` (Trello), `jr:` (Jira), `gh:` (GitHub) and so on for integrations. Users, clients, invoices and time records have plain numbers.\n\n**Workflow**\n- Log time: find the task with `everhour_search_tasks` (or `everhour_list_projects` and `everhour_list_project_tasks`), confirm with the user, then `everhour_add_time`.\n- Timers: `everhour_get_running_timer`, `everhour_start_timer`, `everhour_stop_timer`; `everhour_list_team_timers` shows who is tracking now.\n- Review time: `everhour_list_time_records` (whole team), `everhour_list_user_time_records`, `everhour_list_project_time_records`; ids of people come from `everhour_get_me` and `everhour_list_users`.\n- Billing and planning: `everhour_list_clients`, `everhour_get_project`, `everhour_get_task`, `everhour_list_invoices`, `everhour_get_invoice`, `everhour_list_expenses`, `everhour_list_schedule`, `everhour_projects_report`, `everhour_users_report`.\n- Corrections: `everhour_update_time_record`; `everhour_delete_time_record` only if an admin has switched it on.\n\n**Rate limit**: about 20 requests per 10 seconds per key. A 429 carries `Retry-After` in seconds; wait that long.\n\n**Common errors**\n- 401 or 403 `Access denied`: the API key is wrong, was regenerated, or your role may not see this data (members see only their own time and projects).\n- 404: the id does not exist, or the platform prefix is missing (`ev:123`, not `123`).\n- 422: a required field is missing or the record is locked or already invoiced.\n\n**Out of scope here**: creating or changing projects, tasks, clients, invoices and expenses, timecards (clock in and out), timesheet approvals, time off allocations, custom fields and webhooks.",
  "region": "intl",
  "category": "time-tracking",
  "icon": "everhour",
  "docsUrl": "https://developers.everhour.com/",
  "prerequisites": "An Everhour account and its API token from Settings, My Profile (bottom of the page). About 1 minute.",
  "requiredEnvVars": [
    "EVERHOUR_API_KEY"
  ],
  "envVarMeta": {
    "EVERHOUR_API_KEY": {
      "label": "Everhour API token",
      "kind": "credential",
      "secret": true,
      "help": "app.everhour.com, Settings, My Profile: API Token at the bottom of the page. It acts with your role (admin, supervisor or member).",
      "link": "https://app.everhour.com/#/account/profile",
      "example": "abcd-efgh-1234567-7890ab-cdefgh12",
      "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9-]{16,80}$",
      "patternMessage": "Paste the API token as shown in your profile, letters, digits and dashes only, without spaces."
    }
  },
  "verifyHints": {
    "401": "Everhour refused the API token. Copy it again from Settings, My Profile at https://app.everhour.com/#/account/profile.",
    "403": "Everhour refused the API token (Access denied). Copy it again from Settings, My Profile; a token is replaced when it is regenerated.",
    "429": "Everhour is rate limiting this token. Wait a minute and verify again."
  },
  "probe": {
    "tool": "everhour_get_me",
    "params": {}
  },
  "connector": {
    "name": "Everhour",
    "type": "REST",
    "baseUrl": "https://api.everhour.com",
    "authType": "API_KEY",
